kevin_prod: Hey team — our Node onboarding run is hitting a lot of 429s and some auth failures. Small service, ~200 parallel clients during warmup. Logs show `insufficient_quota` then 429s. Any quick fixes before we flip to prod?

sam_cs: Hi @kevin_prod — can you paste a short snippet of the error + the SDK init code? quick questions: are you doing an ephemeral token per request or per session, and are you preflighting on every tab/client? :thinking_face:

kevin_prod: Paste of logs: 
```
[2026-03-23T14:12:03Z] client=service-a auth=ok token_age=3s request_id=ab12 status=200
[2026-03-23T14:12:03Z] client=service-b auth=failed error=insufficient_quota rev=1
[2026-03-23T14:12:03Z] client=service-c status=429 message="rate limit exceeded"
```
Init snippet: 
```
const sdk = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await sdk.preflight(); // called on every user session open
```
We were following the quickstart which calls preflight aggressively.

sam_cs: Ok — two immediate quick wins: (1) stop doing a full `preflight()` on every session open; cache the result for ~30-60s per process. (2) reduce parallel preflight fanout during onboarding — go from 200 -> 10-20 and splay the calls (random 50-300ms). Add jitter to backoffs. That usually kills the stampede.

ahmad_eng: Adding infra context: we saw a concentrated burst from that API key across ~80 distinct source IPs at 14:12. Default onboarding guard rails throttle ephemeral preflight-heavy patterns to protect shared capacity. For immediate mitigation you can: 
- reuse ephemeral tokens per session (instead of per request)
- limit preflight concurrency to <= 20 per tenant during ramp
- enable http2 keepalives and connection reuse in Node (reduce TCP churn)

Example recommended client change: 
```
// cache preflight for 45s
let _preflight = null;
async function cachedPreflight() {
  if (_preflight && Date.now() - _preflight.ts < 45000) return _preflight.res;
  const res = await sdk.preflight();
  _preflight = { ts: Date.now(), res };
  return res;
}
// splay concurrency
const SPLAY_MS = () => Math.floor(Math.random()*300)+50;
await sleep(SPLAY_MS());
await cachedPreflight();
```

onboard-bot: Rate alert: key=rw_live_•••• saw 429 spike at 2026-03-23T14:12:00Z. Current window: 120s, peak rps=52, avg rps=11. Suggest reducing client concurrency.

kevin_prod: Thanks — patched the init to cache preflight 45s, added splay and lowered parallel warmup to 15. Ran a quick test and 429s dropped significantly (was ~30% of sessions, now ~1-2%). Great.

sam_cs: Nice! Two follow-ups: (1) we'll open a short support ticket to whitelist a temporary warmup window if you need >20 concurrency for a short time (2) can you share the exact client deploy time so we can correlate logs and flip any temporary throttles if needed? Also, here's our docs page on preflight patterns: https://docs.redwood.ai/onboarding/preflight-best-practices — includes examples for browser, node, mobile. :link:

ahmad_eng: If you anticipate steady >50 rps we can propose a Dedicated warmup or reserved burst for the onboarding phase — will coordinate with CS/ops. For now the config above should keep you healthy. We can also add a short-lived increase to the per-key rate for ~10 minutes if you send the ticket.

kevin_prod: We'll run a gradual ramp in prod with the patched splay and keep a 30s preflight cache. I'll file the ticket now and post the ticket id here. Thanks all :raised_hands:

sam_cs: Awesome — ping us the ticket id and we'll triage and coordinate a temporary quota bump if needed. :thumbsup:
